## The Ostwick Gate

::bg{location="ostwick_gate" time="dawn"}
::music{playback="start" mood="upbeat" volume="down"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: Eleven wagons, forty mules, and a strongbox nobody is supposed to know about. East of the gate the Ember Road opens like a wound that never closed.
::actor{character="brannoc" anchor="center" action="fadeInUp"}
@brannoc{code="0010"}: Warden. The Company has paid for three things: the cargo, the road, and you. Get all eleven wagons over the Tollbridge before the fourth night.
@brannoc{code="0020"}: Harrow's Ford is a day out. Past the ford it's Dusk country.
::actor{character="isolde" anchor="left" action="fadeInUp"}
@isolde{code="0010"}: The Duskbound are deserters and hungry farmers, Captain. Not demons.
@brannoc{code="0030"}: Hungry farmers with crossbows, Vane.
::actor{character="corvin" anchor="right" action="fadeInUp"}
@corvin{code="0010"}: And a toll, I hear. Everyone on this road has a toll. Some of us are only more honest about it.

<branch id="orders" prompt="Brannoc waits for your answer.">
  <choice id="swear" text="\"The wagons cross. You have my word.\"">
    @brannoc{code="0040"}: Your word. Good. The Company collects on those.
    ::set{run.rep.company += 1}
    ::use{component="reaction" who="isolde" feel="approves" instance="use-001"}
  </choice>
  <choice id="price" text="For what you pay, the wagons get there. The mules are a maybe.">
    @brannoc{code="0050"}: Funny. Get the mules there too.
    ::use{component="reaction" who="corvin" feel="approves" instance="use-002"}
  </choice>
  <choice id="dusk" text="What did the Company do to the Duskbound?">
    @brannoc{code="0060" emotion="angry"}: Nothing they didn't earn. Mind your road, Warden.
    ::set{run.rep.company -= 1}
    ::use{component="reaction" who="isolde" feel="approves" instance="use-003"}
    @isolde{code="0020"}: A fair question. Notice he didn't answer it.
  </choice>
</branch>

::actor{character="brannoc" action="fadeOut"}
@corvin{code="0020"}: Eleven wagons. You know what's in the twelfth crate of the ninth wagon?
@isolde{code="0030"}: Corvin.
@corvin{code="0030"}: I'm only saying the Company counts to eleven and packs twelve.
@narrator{code="0020"}: The gate grinds open. The Ember Road takes you in.
